# Google Drive for everyone who uses this deployment. These values belong to YOUR Google Cloud
# project; writers never see or enter them (the app has no Google fields). They are baked into the
# bundle at build time, so set them in your host (Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables) as well as in .env.local. See tech_notes.md → "Google Cloud setup".
# Leave them blank to build without Google Drive: the Drive menu items, dialogs and settings are left out.

# OAuth 2.0 Web client ID (Google Auth Platform → Clients). Enable the Google Drive API and add every
# origin the app is served from (http://localhost:5173, your production domain) as an Authorized
# JavaScript origin.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Browser API key for the Google Picker ("Import from Google Drive…", to open existing Google Docs, Word,
# text, Markdown or HTML files). Create it in the same Cloud project as the client ID, enable the
# "Google Picker API", restrict the key to websites http://localhost:5173/* (plus your host's origin)
# and https://docs.google.com/*, and to the Google Picker API only. Blank = no import from Drive.
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# Optional. The Cloud project number the Picker passes as its app id. Leave blank: it is the number at
# the start of the client ID, and it must be the project that owns the client ID.
VITE_GOOGLE_PROJECT_NUMBER=

# Optional. Your Bookshop.org affiliate id (digits). Makes the "Support the developer" book picks
# affiliate links; without it they are plain Bookshop.org links. See tech_notes.md → Support the developer.
VITE_BOOKSHOP_AFFILIATE_ID=
